  "narrative": "The delivered evidence supports three very large, highly precise dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53 loss is associated with much weaker USP7 dependency, and MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency. These estimates are far above the 10% relative clinical-significance threshold and their 95% intervals are well away from the null, so I accept them as meaningful associations in this lung cancer cell-line dataset. KEAP1 loss also produced a very large effect, but in the direction opposite to the pre-specified synthetic-lethal expectation: KEAP1-loss samples were less dependent on NFE2L2, not more. I therefore reject the original H6 claim and register a reversed, dataset-specific hypothesis for follow-up. EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency is borderline: the signed point estimate is just above the 10% threshold, but the interval is close to null, so it remains unresolved and I requested independent validation. KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency and TP53 loss versus MDM2 dependency have point effects below the threshold with intervals that include both null and possible clinical significance, so they remain unresolved with subgroup follow-up. BRAF V600E and MYC-amplification comparisons for DHX9/RPL11/POLR2A show no support for the expected stronger-dependency direction; H2, H10, H11, and H12 are rejected. ERBB2 amplification is inconclusive and deferred. These are associations in the supplied data, not causal or generalizable claims. The strongest possible concern for the large accepted effects is hidden technical or dataset-design confounding; subgroup and CRISPR-library robustness analyses are proposed to test whether the SMARCA2, USP7, and WRN effects persist across biological and technical strata.",
  "research_notes": "Discovery appraisal complete for 12 registered claims. Accepted dataset-specific associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H8 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; H9 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency. H6 rejected as pre-specified: KEAP1 loss is strongly associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; reversed hypothesis proposed. Validation requested for H3 because EGFR amplification effect is near the 10% threshold. Deferred/active borderline: H1 KRAS, H3 EGFR, H7 MDM2, H4 ERBB2. Rejected null/weak claims: H2 BRAF, H10-H12 MYC effects. Next analysis priority: analyze untested H13-H16 if capacity allows, plus reversed H6, EGFR/KRAS/MDM2 subgroup refinements, and robustness of H5/H8/H9 by lineage subtype and CRISPR library. Avoid overgeneralizing: all conclusions are limited to this dataset.",
  "validate": "H3"
}

