ith large signed effects around +0.80 and validated support around +0.81. Third, TP53 loss is associated with markedly weaker dependency_USP7, with full-population, adenocarcinoma, high-screen-quality, high-Cas9, PTEN-loss co-loss, KEAP1-loss, and validated KEAP1-loss contexts supporting the same direction. Fourth, MSI-high status is associated with markedly stronger dependency_WRN, with full-population and several constrained contexts near +0.77 to +0.82. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency_STAT3, with broad and validated robustness in high-quality screens, high-quality high-Cas9 screens, TP53-loss lines, high hypoxia, and now high IFN-gamma signature lines.\n\nNegative or unsupported findings remain: no clinically meaningful full-population effect of KRAS mutation on dependency_KRAS; no clinically meaningful effect of BRAF V600E on dependency_BRAF, including in KRAS-wild-type lines; no meaningful EGFR-amplification effects on dependency_EGFR or dependency_TMED10; no meaningful ERBB2-amplification effects on dependency_ERBB2 or dependency_STAT3; no strong MYC-amplification effects on dependency_DHX9, dependency_RPL11, dependency_POLR2A, or dependency_KIF18A; no clinically meaningful canonical TP53-loss effect on dependency_MDM2; no MSI-high effect on dependency_POLR2A after validation; no stable PTEN-loss effect on dependency_KRAS among KRAS-mutant lines after validation; and no clinically meaningful effects from the constructed research markers D, E, or F.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty remains around effect modification rather than presence of the main associations. The most informative next analyses are the registered interactions testing whether high IFN-gamma signature truly modifies PTEN-loss associated stronger dependency_STAT3 (H141) and whether low Cas9 activity amplifies or attenuates it (H142), because both discovery contexts are strong but need complement comparisons. Also useful pending tests are the high-EMT and high-stemness PTEN-loss 