  "narrative": "No assessments are due, so I do not change any existing claim status. I register a new focused set of comparisons that test biologically interpretable follow-ups to the accepted dataset-specific associations and to earlier null or weak co-driver signals. First, I test whether KRAS mutation is associated with weaker BRAF and weaker EGFR dependency in technically stringent high-quality, high-Cas9 screens. More negative dependency scores mean stronger dependency, so weaker dependency is expected as a positive exposed-minus-comparator contrast. The rationale is that constitutive KRAS activation can bypass upstream receptor or BRAF nodes, reducing apparent dependency on them. Plausible alternatives are no effect or even stronger upstream dependency if MAPK pathway feedback maintains dependence on multiple nodes. Second, I test PTEN loss and KRAS dependency among KRAS-wild-type, high-quality screens. PTEN loss activates PI3K signaling, which may either increase feedback activation of the RAS pathway or bypass KRAS; I hypothesize stronger KRAS dependency, corresponding to a negative exposed-minus-comparator contrast. Third, I test PIK3CA mutation and STAT3 dependency among PTEN-intact high-quality screens to ask whether genetic PI3K pathway activation can phenocopy the accepted PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency. This is a specific pathway-phenocopy hypothesis rather than another PTEN-loss robustness test; a null result would support greater specificity of PTEN loss. Fourth, I test TP53 loss and WRN dependency among MSI-negative, high-quality, high-Cas9 screens. WRN dependency is strongly associated with MSI-high status, so I restrict to MSI-negative lines to ask whether p53-associated replication-stress or checkpoint context adds independent signal. The alternative is that WRN dependency in this dataset is largely MSI-driven and unrelated to TP53 status. Fifth, I test MYC amplification and POLR2A dependency in high-MYC-expression, high-quality lines as a more transcriptional-expression-defined context after broad MYC amplification outcomes were near null. This tests whether MYC amplification has detectable dependency effect only when transcriptional output is also elevated, and also complements active MYC-expression-context DHX9 follow-up. I use approximate 10 percent outcome-scale benchmarks for judgment, roughly: dependency_BRAF and dependency_EGFR and dependency_KRAS about 0.025, dependency_STAT3 about 0.028, dependency_WRN about 0.030, and dependency_POLR2A about 0.025. A discovery will be considered scientifically meaningful if the signed interval lower bound is near or above these thresholds. All proposed claims are observational dataset-specific hypotheses, not causal or generalizable claims.",
