  "narrative": "No assessments are due, so I do not change any existing claim statuses. I register a new set of falsifiable follow-up comparisons rather than refinements, to avoid missing motivating-evidence links and to broaden the evidence base around accepted dataset-specific associations. The WRN proposals ask whether the accepted MSI-high association remains strong in technically stringent screens with mutation burden below the top quartile, and whether it persists in TP53-loss lines. The first would support an MSI-context effect rather than a generic mutation-burden proxy; the second would test whether p53 context coexists with, rather than explains, the MSI signal. The STAT3 proposals test PTEN-loss-associated stronger STAT3 dependency in technically stringent low-IFN-gamma lines, high-MYC-expression lines, and high-AXL-expression lines. These probe whether the broad PTEN-loss/STAT3 association is robust in expression contexts with potentially distinct transcriptional, RTK, inflammatory, or Cas9-quality biology. The KRAS/receptor proposals test pathway-bypass specificity: among KRAS-wild-type high-quality lines, BRAF V600E is expected to show weaker KRAS dependency if downstream activation bypasses KRAS, while EGFR amplification is expected to show stronger KRAS dependency if upstream receptor signaling feeds through RAS. Conversely, among KRAS-mutant lines, EGFR and ERBB2 dependency should be weaker if KRAS mutation bypasses those receptor nodes. The NFE2L2 proposal tests whether the accepted KEAP1-loss-associated weaker dependency persists in TP53-loss lines, where co-loss may change oxidative-stress and p53-associated survival biology. The non-Avana high-quality robustness tests ask whether the very strong SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 and TP53-loss/USP7 associations survive in screens with a different library, controlling for high screen ROC quality. I use approximate 10% population-scale dependency-score benchmarks for each outcome. For dependency_STAT3 and dependency_USP7, a benchmark is about 0.028; for dependency_KRAS, dependency_EGFR, dependency_BRAF, and dependency_WRN, about 0.025-0.030; for dependency_SMARCA2 and dependency_NFE2L2, the effects are expected to be very large if real. A proposal will be considered scientifically meaningful only if the signed estimate and lower interval bound support the registered direction near or above these thresholds. All claims remain observational within the supplied dataset and are not interpreted as causal or generalizable.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 explore repair: no assessments due, so accepted set unchanged. Avoided parent links because previous refinement attempts lacked available motivating result IDs. New proposals target: WRN MSI effect below top-quartile mutation burden and WRN MSI effect in TP53 loss; PTEN-loss STAT3 under stringent low-IFN, high-MYC-expression, and high-AXL-expression contexts; KRAS dependency modified by BRAF mutation or EGFR amplification in KRAS-wild-type high-quality lines; EGFR/ERBB2 dependency among KRAS-mutant lines under bypass expectations; KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 in TP53-loss lines; non-Avana high-quality robustness for SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 and TP53-loss USP7. Existing accepted core: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2, TP53 loss with weaker USP7, MSI-high with stronger WRN, and PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 across many contexts. Existing negative/unsupported: broad KRAS mutation effect on dependency_KRAS, BRAF V600E on dependency_BRAF, EGFR/ERBB2 amplification main effects, broad MYC amplification outcomes, TP53-loss MDM2, MSI-POLR2A validation, PTEN-KRAS validation among KRAS mutants, and research markers D/E/F for tested outcomes. Active unresolved interaction/context claims remain H149, H150, H151, and H152. No new voluntary validation requests remain; scheduled validation may still arrive. All conclusions are dataset-specific observational associations."
